# Pinned sha256 hashes for the didc release archives listed in `.didc-release`.
#
# Kept in lockstep with `.didc-release` so the helper in
# `scripts/didc-helpers.bash` can verify each downloaded archive before
# executing the binary inside it — without this, the download path is
# plain HTTPS-with-no-integrity-check (caught by the ZeroPath static-
# analysis ruleset that guards against unverified-binary-execution
# patterns).
#
# `scripts/update-deps/update-didc` refreshes these together with
# `.didc-release`. The format is one `<target> <sha256>` pair per line
# (whitespace-separated, comments allowed); targets must match the
# `didc-<target>.tar.xz` asset names on the dfinity/candid release page.
#
# To recompute by hand:
#   release=$(sed <.didc-release 's/#.*$//' | sed '/^$/d')
#   for target in aarch64-apple-darwin x86_64-apple-darwin aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu; do
#     curl -sfL "https://github.com/dfinity/candid/releases/download/$release/didc-$target.tar.xz" \
#       | shasum -a 256 | awk -v t="$target" '{print t, $1}'
#   done

